        "49": "For \\(f(x) = 1/x\\), second divided difference over \\(a, b, c\\) simplifies to \\(f[a, b, c] = \frac{1}{abc}\\).",
        "50": "Picard iterations: \\(y_0=1, y_1 = 1 - x + \frac{x^2}{2}, y_2 = 1 + x^2 - x - \frac{x^3}{6}\\). At \\(x=0.2, y_2 \approx 0.8387\\).",
        "61": "Expanding the determinant shows it equals \\(12 \cdot f[1, 2, 5]\\). Given determinant 60, \\(f[1, 2, 5] = 60/12 = 5\\).",
        "62": "Form forward-difference table (\\(h=10\\)); second differences are constant (\\(2\\)) so extrapolate to \\(x=100\\) to get \\(f(100) = 15\\).",
        "63": "Simpson's three-eighth rule assumes cubic on each subinterval block and Trapezoidal rule works for any (finite) number of equal subintervals — both statements are true.",
        "64": "Use Newton's forward interpolation on the grouped marks table: build the forward-difference table for class midpoints and interpolate the count between 60 and 70.",
