        "66": "Compute divided differences: \\(f[1, 2] = 6, f[2, 4] = 125, f[1, 2, 4] = \frac{125-6}{4-1} = \frac{119}{3}\\). Plug into Newton form to get \\(f(3) \approx 92\\).",
        "67": "Forward difference of polynomial: \\(\Delta(6x^3) = 18x^2 + 18x + 6, \Delta(3x^2) = 6x + 3, \Delta(2x) = 2\\). Sum gives \\(18x^2 + 24x + 11\\).",
        "68": "Apply Euler's explicit step four times: \\(y_{n+1} = y_n + h(x_n + y_n)\\). Carrying out the iterations gives \\(y_4 \approx 0.0641\\) at \\(x = 0.4\\).",
