        "23": "Operators here cancel on the exponential: acting on \\(e^x\\) the factor and its reciprocal produce the identity, so the product equals \\(e^x\\).",
        "24": "Trapezoid on \\([0, 1]\\): \\(\frac{1}{2}(1.1 + 2.4) = 1.75\\). Simpson on \\([1, 2]\\) with \\(h=0.5\\): \\(\frac{0.5}{3}(2.4 + 4 \cdot 5.7 + 8.1) = 5.55\\). Total \\(I = 7.30\\).",
        "25": "Ansatz \\(y = 2^x(ax^2 + bx + c)\\). Solving \\((E-8)y = x^2 2^x\\) gives \\(a = -1/6, b = -1/9, c = -5/54\\), so \\(y = -\frac{2^x}{54}(9x^2 + 6x + 5)\\).",
